meta {
  name: Create PAN card (auto-verify)
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/pan
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "panNumber": "{{plutusPanNumber}}",
    "holderName": "Test Owner"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.statusCode: eq 200
  res.body.data.id: isNumber
  res.body.data.panNumber: eq {{plutusPanNumber}}
}

script:post-response {
  bru.setVar("plutusPanCardId", res.body.data.id);
}

docs {
  `PANCardResource.createPANCard` (VAHN_ADMIN, TORG_ADMIN) -> `PANCardService.createPANCard`. Body is
  `PANCardDTO` (`panNumber` ^[A-Z]{5}[0-9]{4}[A-Z]$ required; `holderName` falls back to the user's name;
  `phone`, `isSoleProprietor`, `businessName`, `documentUrl` optional). Surepass is tried first; on
  failure the PAN stays PENDING. statusCode 400 "PAN Card already exists for the torg" in the body (so the asserts below need an owner without a PAN) if the caller's torg already
  has a primary PAN. Since BUG-108 a VERIFIED result recomputes the owner's onboarding status.
  The HTTP status is always 200; read `statusCode` in the body. Needs `plutusPanNumber` (a fresh PAN).
  See flows/plutus-api/kyc-onboarding-status for the full journey.
}
